next tuesday the house commons is going  to vote on a new set of measures to  restrict the spread of covert we've just  been hearing from the secretary of state  are you going to support your government  well i'm expecting four votes i will  vote against vaccine passports i'll vote  against extending a face mask mandate  i'll vote against uh mandatory  vaccination as a condition of nhs  employment the fourth one is a slightly  liberalizing measure i don't expect the  house to divide but yes i will vote  against i think what we're doing now is  creating a miserable dystopia that into  which we're going forward and that's why  today i'm announcing that i'll be  relaunching conservative way forward we  need to create a movement which actually  says the conservative party needs to be  what people traditionally have  recognized as conservative that is in  favor of freedom and personal  responsibility so i hope people will go  to conservativewayforward.com  and sign up as supporters and they'll be  the first to hear more  presumably you wouldn't be launching  this if you didn't have some support  do you have any idea how many members of  parliament will join you uh from the  conservative benches in voting against  the government on tuesday  well the spectator has run a list on  this and they've got 65 names on there  it's not absolutely clear to me that  they'll all vote against some may  abstain but i know about half a dozen  extra names so it feels to me that it's  going to be at least 60 people voting  against but of course it's a foregone  conclusion because our useless  opposition in name only uh will continue  to support the government however  authoritarian they are but you know  really this is a moment where every last  one of us should in good faith start  thinking about what it means with to  live with coronavirus like we live with  flu now that we're vaccinated and what  kind of society we want to live in in  the future i want one which is free  which is prosperous and which is joyful  in which young people can have a hope of  a better future and at the moment when  we're not looking like we're going to  deliver that if we keep on panicking  every time we get a variant this disease  will now be with us forever there will  be new variants the vaccine continues to  give a high degree of protection against  serious illness and death and in  straight we just do now need to get on  with our lives  we read this morning in the newspapers  about dissent in the cabinet and the  possibility that  ministers may resign what do you know  about that do you anticipate ministerial  resignations over  these measures  well i i don't know i mean so far  ministers have voted for a great many  things that they don't like doing and  that's been one of the hallmarks of this  period of the coronavirus you know we  keep doing that which we hate but saying  we'd like to be doing something else  well i'm afraid sooner or later if we're  going to save the soul of the  conservative party we've got to actually  do those things which we love to do and  that means being courageous and  temperate and prudent and think counting  the cost of lockdowns and restrictions  rather than having this endless tunnel  vision just on the disease you know we  we actually can't go on like this  only the conservative party can provide  good quality government that that draws  on the tradition of freedom and  responsibility under the rule of law and  all the time we have minute and  frequently changing rules governing our  lives so that we can't plan forward  whether it's for business or for  pleasure i'm afraid we're going to make  enormous swathes of our economy  uninvestable and they'll be just the  swathes which give our lives meaning  things like being able to go on holiday  being able to go to hospitality venues  you know we saw for a long time that  weddings were in trouble you know these  things really matter in our lives and  pretty soon we're going to have to start  learning why it is that we've always  believed in this country that freedom  under the rule of law mattered and  that's really why i'm re-launching  conservative way forward we've got to  show that there is a movement for that  frame of mind because if we don't the  conservative party will continue to  drift into authoritarianism and i simply  cannot stand idly by while that happens  you um  you referred in a newspaper article this  morning to uh the conservative party  essentially and you've repeated it here  having lost its soul is that  what the johnson administration is doing  burying  the conservative uh soul as you  understand it  well at the moment it we're in a pretty  bad shape you know boris did promise us  that he'd be as he put it a brexitee  hezer and that is what he's done he's a  highly interventionist prime minister i  think we did expect that he had two  really important jobs to do he had to  take us out of the european union albeit  with the unfinished business of the  northern ireland protocol and he had to  make sure he beat jeremy corbyn but i'm  afraid i did expect him to spend quite a  lot of money but i think that the thing  that's really changed now is we've used  so much quantitative easing that is  money creation to cover the enormous  amount of borrowing the government has  had to get us through covid i think now  as we go forward we've got to be  extremely careful to apply conservative  principles to what we do because the  size of the state the size of taxation  is now not consistent with conservative  government it's a it would be you know  fit for a miliband government and much  as i'm on friendly terms with ed  miliband i didn't want to be in his  party  mr baker what what's interesting about  the way you talk about this is that um  you're not talking about it really  as a partisan or even an economic  question  you seem to be posing  the issue as a moral one and that in  some way where the conservative party is  now  is in some sense immoral  in a sense almost ethical or religious  is that your belief  well if i were to to put it to you as  plainly as i can surely life for each of  us is a process of becoming it's a  process of becoming greater tomorrow  than we were today not of comparing  ourselves to other people but comparing  ourselves to what we were and trying to  become better in some sense now if life  is a process of becoming don't we  deserve the dignity of choice as free  human beings with something like a soul  and if you don't have any kind of  spiritual belief well at least come up  with something which gives you meaning  as a freely choosing individual i mean  where are we going to find meaning and  purpose in our lives if we don't have  choice and responsibility and this  opportunity to grow and so that's why  i'm so very concerned that what is  happening here is we're being treated by  the government by the public health  establishment as automata who can't  manage to decide for themselves that  it's a good idea to wear a mask in an  enclosed space i think we've all learned  that now i'm certainly capable of doing  it freely and i'm very sure that your  viewers are capable of doing it too and  really we do need to think very  carefully now about what we wish to  become you know in society are our  relationships healthy when they're  voluntary or do they all need to be  coerced i mean this is a fundamental  question  i the reason i um  frame this or raise this as a moral  question is  partly as you said it's to do with  the question of individual choice but  morality also relates to leadership and  i want to ask you  about the leadership that you have  supported of your party and of the  government that you've supported uh  boris johnson this week um essentially  has been in a whole series of issues  about whether he has told us the whole  truth about payments for uh decoration  flats the issue of the again once again  of christmas parties and and so on  do you think  that  this leadership  uh remains the sort of if i like could  put it this way moral leadership that  you can continue to support or does this  prime minister has this prime minister  reach the end of the road for you  well i'm really clear that i want boris  johnson to be a success i'll never  forget sitting next to him at dinner i  see it in my mind's eye now and he  started to talk about the condition and  the prosperity of the british people in  a way which was earnest and honest yeah  but if i forgive me if i may interrupt  boris johnson i want to see  yeah forgive me though uh  boris johnson's idea of success may not  be exactly the same as yours and what  you seem to be saying here is that uh  success is not just a matter of winning  or getting through it or getting past  the next scandal it is also about what  you believe and how you behave so let me  ask you again  is boris johnson  still the kind of leader behaving in the  kind of way this uh displaying the kind  of morals that you feel  that the conservative party should still  support  i i think right now the prime minister  is in very great difficulty for the  reasons that you're indicating any  member of the public is going to rightly  demand that politicians not only comply  with the rules that they impose on other  people but that they're seen to comply  with their spirit and it's pretty  obvious now that that hasn't happened  and that is it that is a very bad  position to be in but let me be clear  trevor i've been down this road once  before viewers will know and i have  absolutely no intention this time around  of trying to remove a prime minister i  want to see boris turn this situation  around i want to see him rescue his  position i want to see him go on to be a  great success but he's not going to do  it by paying lip service to rules and  being in cautious about how his staff  behave and comply with them so you know  we don't make him prime minister for his  meticulous attention to detail but you  know it is now time a time for complete  compliance with all rules  so you're clear he hasn't followed the  rules if he doesn't turn it around  within let's say a few months is it  going to be time for him to go  well trevor as i just said a moment ago  and i hope you will understand and your  viewers will understand i've been down  this road before and i'm determined not  to go down it again the reason that i'm  launching conservative relaunching in  the new year conservative way forward is  because i think we need to create a  movement which says to boris and the  whole conservative party we want to live  in a society characterized by freedom  under the rule of law and personal  responsibility that's really what i'm  about  steve baker thank you very much indeed

